course: dictionary
lesson: 3302
title: Ethical: fair and right
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ethical means morally right, fair and honest. It helps us decide what we should do, not just what we can do. Look at the clues around the word. «Ethical hackers are hired with written permission to test systems» tells you the work is allowed and fair, because the people who own the system said yes.
explain: Sometimes ethical is about thinking, not doing. «The ethical question should be put in one clear sentence» means a question about right and wrong. Ask yourself: is this fair, honest and kind? Then check the meaning by swapping it in: "a fair and honest question should be put in one clear sentence" still makes sense.
explain: Ethical can also describe buying. Ethical shopping means buying things made fairly, without harming workers, animals or nature. A good check is to ask, "Would this still be fair if I could see how it was made?"
fact: Ethical means morally right, fair and honest.
fact: «Ethical» can also mean about right and wrong, as in «an ethical question».
fact: Ethical shopping means buying things made fairly, without harming workers, animals or nature.
fact: «Ethical hackers» are experts hired with written permission to find weak spots so they can be fixed.
fact: Permission is what makes the work legal. An ethical choice is one that is fair and honest, even when nobody is watching.
exercise: «The ethical question should be put in one clear sentence.» What does ethical mean here? | About the weather | *About right and wrong | About money only | About sport
exercise: What does ethical shopping mean? | Buying the cheapest things, whatever they cost | Buying lots of things at once | Shopping only on Sundays | *Buying things made fairly, without harming workers, animals or nature
exercise: «Ethical hackers are hired with written permission to test systems.» What makes their work legal? | Green text on the screen | Ten seconds of typing | Films about hackers | *Written permission
test: Which is an ethical choice? | Copying homework and saying it is yours | *Telling the shop when you get too much change back | Breaking a promise just for fun | Taking a friend's sweets without asking
test: «Real security work is slow and careful, and the legal kind is done by ethical hackers.» Who does the legal kind of security work? | People in films | Thieves who want to steal | Anyone who likes computers, without asking | *Ethical hackers hired with written permission
exam: Why does an ethical hacker need written permission? | *Because permission makes the work legal and fair | Because it makes the screen turn green | Because films say so | Because it makes the work quicker
